import Mathlib



/-! # Kernel-checked orbit classification of matching triples

A hypothetical three-colour solution supplies one nonzero monochromatic perfect
matching per colour, so the object to classify is the triple of matchings.  `K6`
has fifteen perfect matchings, giving `15^3 = 3375` triples, and `S_6 x S_3` acts
by permuting vertices and relabelling colours.

Every triple carries an explicit witness: a vertex permutation and a colour
permutation taking it to its orbit representative.  `classification_correct`
rechecks all 3375 witnesses in the kernel, with no appeal to compiled
evaluation. -/

